That setup is fine with one tweak. In the Mini App read the id from Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe.user.id and send it in the JSON body as before. To make it tamper-proof, compute an HMAC of the body in the browser and send it along:

```js
const BOT_TOKEN = "123456:ABC..."; // used to sign requests
const userId = Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe.user.id;
const sig = await hmacSha256(BOT_TOKEN, JSON.stringify({ userId }));
fetch("/api/orders", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify({ userId, sig }) });
```

On the Express side keep reading req.body.userId and just check it is a number.
